+## Changed
+
+- Replaced task 1's placeholder keep with the real one: the selected entries' paths and rename sources become `openspec/manual/<stamp>.md`, written through `write_frontmatter`, with sorted capabilities from `read_capability_ownership` and `owner_capabilities`.
+- Added the commit path: `resolve_author`, the subject-plus-body commit message, the author fallback, record removal when git refuses, the `Kept ... as ...` line and the `Left out untracked` line.
+- Copied the UTC millisecond formatter into `crates/features/manual/src/time.rs`, and resolved `ManualFeature::new()`'s clock at each keep.
+- Changed the refusals to return both the status snapshot and the selected entries, so the keep can compute the untracked entries it leaves out.
+- Added `tests/manual_keeps.rs` for every keep golden, the planner reading the `folder-prefix` record, and the UTC formatter's fixed times; added `tests/support/mod.rs::kept_records` and `crates/apps/cli/tests/manual_command.rs` for `manual` through `features()`.
+- Added `osq-kernel-specs`, `osq-kernel-storage` and `yaml-rust2` to the crate's manifest, which also updated `Cargo.lock`.
+- `cargo fmt --all`, clippy with `-D warnings`, this task's verify, the proposal's verify, and cargo-mutants over the crate's source files all pass; the mutation run caught every viable mutant (165 caught, 10 unviable, 0 missed).
+
+## Deviated
+
+- `Cargo.lock` changed as cargo resolved the manifest's new kernel and YAML dependencies; it is a generated file outside the task's listed scope.
